/* Deep lessons — Data structures (data-structures).
 *
 * Every structure here exists to make one operation cheap, and each one pays
 * for that somewhere else. So the question this track keeps asking is not
 * "how is it built" but "what does it make cheap, and what did that cost".
 *
 * The pictures carry the relationships a row of boxes cannot: which range a
 * segment tree node owns, which indices one Fenwick counter covers, which set
 * an element belongs to, which slot a key hashed into, which end of a deque is
 * moving. Those relationships are the whole subject.
 *
 * Original text and diagrams. Nothing copied from any source.
 */

import type { DeepLesson } from "../deep-lesson";

